\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The internal factor of a lattice Dirac operator}
\date{2026-11-13}

\p{Mathematical physics writes #{\Gamma_j=\gamma_j\otimes I_F}, a
gamma matrix on the spinor factor and an identity on the internal
factor. The [centered Dirac operator](fdip-000R) writes its
represented generator as #{\rho(\iota(\varepsilon_j))}. Set
#{\varepsilon_j^{S}=\rho(\iota(\varepsilon_j))} on the spinor
factor and #{\bbI_F} on the internal factor. The #{\rho} in that
equation is the representation written in the centered Dirac
operator. The internal representation is the one in the
[covariant centered differences](fdip-009O). The grid step is
already #{e_j}.}
